# Files not to upload when deploying. Vercel builds the site itself, so
# shipping the built output is pure waste — and it is not harmless waste: each
# `vercel --prod` was uploading the ~976 files in dist/, which burned through the
# free tier's 5000-file-per-day upload allowance in about ten deploys and then
# refused to deploy at all for 24 hours.
#
# .gitignore already lists dist/, but the CLI was clearly still picking it up, so
# this file states it explicitly rather than relying on that fallback.
#
# Prefer `vercel --prod --archive=tgz` as well: it uploads a single tarball
# instead of one request per file, which sidesteps the file-count limit entirely.

dist/
node_modules/
.astro/

# Pipeline working directory — regenerable, and pilot-raw.json alone is ~2MB.
data-work/

# Python tooling that only ever runs locally. The build needs the two .mjs
# checks (npm prebuild calls them), so those are NOT excluded.
scripts/*.py

*.log
.env
.env.production
.vercel
.git/
